# .github/CODEOWNERS — module ownership map (Dabbler module-organized projects).
#
# Scaffolded by the Dabbler AI Orchestration extension. GitHub requests a
# review from the matching owners whenever a PR touches their paths (later
# rules win over earlier ones). Docs:
# https://docs.github.com/articles/about-code-owners
#
# Comment-only as scaffolded — nothing is routed until you uncomment a rule.
#
# HOW TO ADAPT: one rule per entry in a module's `codeRoots` in
# docs/modules.yaml, mapping that path to the module's owner(s) — a module
# owning several unrelated paths needs one rule each. A module with a
# `touches:` list composes another module's code, so name that module's owner
# on the rule too — the owner of the code being composed should see it before
# it lands.
#
# WORKED EXAMPLE — the two modules from the Hello World tutorial. Priya owns
# `greeter`; Sam owns `app`, which declares `touches: [greeter]`, so Priya is
# named on it as well. Uncomment both lines and replace the handles with real
# GitHub usernames — GitHub silently declines to route reviews to handles that
# do not exist.
#
# /services/greeter/  @priya-gh
# /services/app/      @sam-gh @priya-gh
#
# On a larger repo, also give every module owner a rule on the files they all
# depend on — docs/modules.yaml and .github/ are the usual conflict magnets.
